"1s1rqkt": "Your ticks are saved only in this browser.",
"1p0eu1l": "In the calculator",
"b54pd6": "Calculate mine",
"qbztnl": "General research-based information, not medical advice and not a substitute for a doctor. Before a significant change, especially with an illness or medication, talk to a professional.",
"kfi2v3": "Keep reading",
"12y8j21": "About the site",
"1ftdotp": "How it works",
"1xjilsr": "Each guide is based on studies published in medical journals and on guidelines from bodies such as the World Health Organization. Every number on the site links to its source, and the numbers were checked against the studies' own abstracts. When a study is observational, meaning it shows an association and not necessarily a cause, that is stated.",
"1i20p98": "The calculator",
"1ablpns": "The starting point is the World Health Organization life table by country, age and sex. Each risk factor is translated into a hazard ratio from a large study and multiplies the death rate at every age. The effect weakens at older ages, and related factors count with reduced weight so the same thing is not counted twice. The result is shown as a range, because nobody can know a date.",
"ecc09t": "Privacy",
"1qjhql5": "No data is sent to any server. The calculation and the reading of blood test and watch files all happen in your browser. If you choose to remember your data, it is stored only in this browser, and you can delete it at any time with the \"Delete my data\" button at the bottom of the page.",
"1yz8i31": "What it is not",
"6043k0": "It is not a diagnosis and not medical advice. The studies describe averages of large groups, not the future of any one person. For any question about your health, talk to your doctor.",
"btxntw": "To the calculator",
"wnj9pj": "You've ticked",
"zfdpwc": "of",
