"11jqlks": "How much sleep you really need, and what to do when you can't fall asleep.",
"1c61mi": "Sleep is not wasted time. Adults need at least 7 hours a night, regularly, and the link between short sleep and mortality shows up in large studies. The good news: chronic sleep problems have an effective treatment without medication.",
"zfm07j": "hours",
"d1ckh9": "The recommendation for adults, according to the AASM and SRS consensus statement",
"zf9e5h": "higher",
"1lc2h47": "mortality risk for people who sleep too little, in a meta-analysis of 16 studies",
"1cjulfk": "first-line treatment",
"1xu4vv4": "CBT-I, cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia, is the first-line treatment for insomnia",
"9sfpss": "How many hours",
"1tuhts": "According to the consensus statement of the American Academy of Sleep Medicine and the Sleep Research Society (2015), a healthy adult needs at least 7 hours of sleep a night. 6 hours or less is not enough to maintain health and safety.",
"7g3hzd": "In Cappuccio's meta-analysis (2010), short sleep was linked to 12% higher mortality risk, and very long sleep to 30%. Very long sleep is often a sign of illness rather than its cause, so this is not a recommendation to sleep less.",
"73hb87": "Regularity matters as much as quantity",
"1wxgcl": "A fixed wake-up time, weekends included, is the anchor of the body clock. If you want to go to bed earlier, it is better to shift gradually, a quarter of an hour at a time.",
"1xh9tmm": "When sleep won't come",
"votytp": "According to the American College of Physicians guideline (2016), the first treatment for chronic insomnia is cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT-I), before medication. It is available face to face, in a group, through an app or from a book. Loud snoring, pauses in breathing or severe daytime tiredness are a reason to see your doctor.",
"f7kgmy": "A fixed wake-up time, seven days a week",
"1lt1cdn": "Choose one time and fit your bedtime around it.",
"xg81k7": "A dark, quiet, comfortable bedroom",
"zjiwvp": "Blackout curtains or an eye mask, a comfortable temperature.",
"pwa3h0": "The phone stays out of bed",
"18hxyao": "Better outside the room altogether, with an ordinary alarm clock.",
"rgpknm": "No caffeine in the afternoon",
"1ltt5it": "And no heavy meal or alcohol in the hours before bed.",
"1apbj3h": "Movement and daylight in the morning",
"17o6m3v": "Physical activity during the day helps you fall asleep at night.",
"13o2sn2": "You can \"catch up\" on sleep at the weekend",
"1ax220z": "Catching up helps you feel better, but irregular sleep disrupts the body clock. A steady amount every night is better.",
"pfwgir": "A sleeping pill is the answer to insomnia",
"q9e4hm": "The professional guideline recommends starting with cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT-I), before medication.",
"2bh2s5": "In the calculator: hours of sleep a night (Cappuccio 2010).",
"12pg9h": "AASM and SRS: recommended sleep duration for adults (2015)",
"mpwf6y": "Cappuccio 2010: sleep duration and mortality (Sleep)",
"rtzg8c": "ACP: management of chronic insomnia (Qaseem 2016)",
"1quzwm7": "CDC: sleep",
"wttii6": "Nutrition",
"1tlxbqa": "What goes on the plate: vegetables, whole grains, less salt, and a Mediterranean direction.",
"1iwlfr6": "According to the Global Burden of Disease study, poor diet was linked to 11 million deaths worldwide in 2017. The top three factors were not \"forbidden foods\" but simple things: too much salt, too few whole grains and too little fruit.",
