"1jzr2p9": "Holt-Lunstad 2010: social relationships and mortality (PLoS Med)",
"zavk0j": "Smoking and alcohol",
"esqb4d": "How many years quitting smoking gives back, and where the line is with alcohol.",
"1b1xh88": "Smoking is the biggest risk factor you can change: smokers lose more than a decade. But it is never too late to quit, and even people who quit at 50 gain back many years.",
"xppf9f": "of life expectancy lost by smokers compared with people who never smoked",
"wt4af7": "gained by people who quit at 45–54, compared with those who continue",
"384mbg": "grams",
