"1q2fsl7": "Smoking: it's never too late",
"ybw71p": "In Jha's study (NEJM 2013) of more than 200,000 Americans, smokers lost more than 10 years of life. Those who quit at 25–34 gained about 10 years, at 35–44 about 9 years, and at 45–54 about 6 years, compared with those who continued. Quitting before 40 removed about 90% of the excess risk.",
"jvm094": "Doctors, pharmacies and national quitlines offer support and stop-smoking medication. Combining support with medication raises the chance of success.",
"1mgmo4r": "Alcohol: less is better",
"p8licd": "In an analysis of about 600,000 drinkers (Wood, Lancet 2018), the lowest mortality risk was at up to about 100 grams of pure alcohol a week, roughly 6 glasses of wine of 175 ml. People who drank more than 350 grams a week lost about 4–5 years of life expectancy at age 40.",
"xqjwgl": "The Global Burden of Disease study (2018) concluded that the level that minimizes overall health harm is zero. There is no reason to start drinking \"for your health\".",
