"1v84m9g": "A high-quality diet",
"11kqlaa": "According to the consensus statement of the American Academy of Sleep Medicine and the Sleep Research Society (2015), a healthy adult needs at least 7 hours of sleep a night, regularly. Sleeping 6 hours or less is not enough to maintain health and safety. The statement did not set an upper limit.",
"126799h": "Included in the calculation: short sleep raises the risk by 12%, and very long sleep by 30% (Cappuccio 2010). Very long sleep is sometimes a sign of illness rather than its cause, so this is not a recommendation to sleep less.",
"16uwlkp": "A fixed wake-up time, weekends included",
"19g35xp": "Choose one wake-up time and fit your bedtime around it. If you need to make it earlier, do it gradually.",
"1j10cd9": "A quiet, dark, comfortable bedroom",
"1srtlh4": "Blackout curtains or an eye mask, a comfortable temperature, and the phone and screens out of bed, preferably out of the room altogether.",
