"8xw8pq": "The World Health Organization recommends at least 400 grams of vegetables and fruit a day (about five servings, not counting potatoes and cassava), less than 10% of energy from free sugars (under 5% gives extra benefit), and less than 5 grams of salt a day. In Aune's meta-analysis (2017), each additional 200 grams of vegetables and fruit a day is linked to about 10% lower mortality, with the benefit continuing up to 800 grams a day and the biggest improvement among those who eat very little.",
