Object.assign(I18N.en, {
"1ayycaa": "Go by how it feels to you. If you have a VO2max measurement from a fitness watch, it is used instead.",
"qftz4e": "Obstructive sleep apnoea is repeated pauses in breathing during the night. In the meta-analysis by Fu (2017), 27 cohort studies, severe apnoea was linked to about 2.1 times the risk of death from any cause compared with people without apnoea (HR 2.13, 95% confidence interval: 1.68–2.68). The comparison by severity was based on 11 studies, and the authors note publication bias and only partial adjustment for risk factors in some studies. For mild (1.19) and moderate (1.28) apnoea the link was not statistically significant.",
"16pm158": "In the meta-analysis by Benjafield (2025), 30 studies, ten of them randomised trials, positive airway pressure treatment (PAP, including CPAP) was linked to 37% lower all-cause mortality compared with no treatment or little use (HR 0.63, 95% confidence interval: 0.56–0.72). In the randomised trials alone the result was 0.87 (0.65–1.16), which was not statistically significant. The overall significance came from non-randomised studies, so part of the difference may be due to other differences between people who are treated and people who are not. A trend toward greater benefit with more use was seen, but the difference was not significant. The authors describe this as a possible effect, and the study was funded by ResMed, a maker of PAP devices.",
"vjx8hv": "The American Academy of Sleep Medicine guideline (Sateia 2017) suggests, as a weak recommendation, not using melatonin, valerian or tryptophan to treat chronic insomnia in adults, compared with no treatment. The recommendation on melatonin was based on trials of 2 mg, including three trials only in adults over 55, and the quality of evidence for it was rated very low. A weak recommendation reflects lower certainty, and does not mean the supplement does not work. According to other Academy guidelines on which this guideline relies, anyone with chronic insomnia should receive CBT-I as the first treatment."
});
Object.assign(I18N.en, {
"wetsbq": "Which products do you use? You can tick several.",
"189b3jl": "Cigarettes",
"h9mjau": "Rolling tobacco or pipe",
"br05t4": "Hookah (narghile)",
"1i0gopd": "E-cigarette",
"1rmnhi2": "Heated tobacco",
"z5pbqp": "Roughly how many cigarettes a day? (If you do not smoke cigarettes, you can skip)",
"39i34x": "Based on your answers. This is general research-based information, not a diagnosis and not a substitute for a doctor. The coach is for people aged 18 and over.",
"1em1k8n": "This coach is for people aged 18 and over. If you are younger and you smoke or use nicotine, it is worth talking to your doctor, a counsellor or an adult you trust. You can quit, and you can get help.",
"1edt233": "In pregnancy and breastfeeding, quitting smoking matters, and help is available. Support through talking is recommended, and on nicotine replacement and medicines it is worth deciding with a doctor or midwife, because there is currently not enough evidence on the safety or benefit of medicines in pregnancy. It is worth reaching out early, even if quitting is hard.",
"n9v4vq": "If you have heart disease, talk to a doctor before nicotine replacement or medicines. In the Cochrane review, more chest pain and palpitations were recorded with nicotine replacement, and they are rare.",
"1dholwt": "If you take psychiatric medicines or are being treated for a mental health condition, talk to your doctor before you start. After quitting smoking, the effect of medicines and your mood may need to be monitored.",
"1xedgcc": "Based on your answers, it is worth involving a doctor from the start. This is not a diagnosis, but a general recommendation when there are signs of strong nicotine dependence (heavy smoking, first cigarette early in the morning) or when earlier attempts were difficult.",
"1tcazsf": "In an American study by Jha (NEJM, 2013), people who quit smoking at age 25–34 gained about 10 years, at 35–44 about 9, at 45–54 about 6 and at 55–64 about 4, compared with those who continued. Quitting before age 40 avoided about 90% of the excess risk of death.",
"12mieu6": "Professional support raises the chance of quitting. In Cochrane reviews, individual counselling raised the chance of quitting by about 1.6 times compared with minimal contact, and combining support with medicine raised it by about 1.8 times compared with brief advice or usual care. These are risk ratios, not the success rate itself. You can choose what suits you: a meeting, a group or phone calls.",
"5bamnq": "Nicotine replacement and medicines in pregnancy",
"125g46m": "In pregnancy and breastfeeding there is no general recommendation here on nicotine replacement or medicines. The decision is made with a doctor or midwife, and in the meantime support through talking is a step you can start with.",
"1wgwr6c": "Nicotine replacement (patches, gum, lozenges) raised the chance of quitting by about 1.5 times compared with not using it (a risk ratio). Combining a patch with a fast-acting form worked better than one form. It is worth asking a pharmacist or doctor how to use them.",
"x2am7c": "There are also prescription medicines for quitting. In reviews they were found effective, and some are more effective than a single form of nicotine replacement, but they have not been shown to be better than combined nicotine replacement. They suit only some people, so this is a conversation with a doctor about suitability and safety. It is an ordinary question, and you can ask it without worry. We do not recommend a specific medicine or dose.",
"165bjfv": "Set a day and tell people",
"1sbnj91": "You can set a quit day in the coming weeks and tell family and friends. The first days are usually harder: strong cravings, irritability, and difficulty concentrating or sleeping are withdrawal symptoms that fade gradually, and there is treatment for them. It is worth keeping the home and car smoke-free, also to protect those around you.",
"7kvtd0": "If you slip",
"kqxrsb": "A slip does not cancel what you have achieved so far, and you can try again. It is worth talking to a counsellor or doctor. One medicine was tested for preventing relapse and found helpful, not all medicines, while an additional behavioural programme alone has not been shown to add anything.",
"3wvhzo": "Hookah, e-cigarettes and other tobacco",
"1hg7ra": "Most of the studies presented here were done on cigarette smokers, and there is less information on other products. Hookah, e-cigarettes and heated tobacco usually contain nicotine and can create dependence. Support, a quit day and coping with the hard moments are relevant for them too, and you can talk to a doctor.",
"1edhgw0": "If during quitting you get chest pain, severe shortness of breath, or thoughts of harming yourself, see a doctor, and in an emergency go to the emergency room or call the ambulance service."
});
Object.assign(I18N.en, {
"yo141m": "If you take psychiatric medicines or are being treated for a mental health condition, talk to your doctor before you start. After quitting smoking, the blood levels of some medicines may change, so monitoring may be needed. Mood changes may also appear, and your doctor should guide you.",
"1rhug38": "Based on your answers, it is worth involving a doctor from the start. This is not a diagnosis, but a general recommendation when there are signs of strong nicotine dependence (heavy smoking, first cigarette early in the morning) or when earlier attempts were difficult. If you had severe withdrawal symptoms in the past, it is better not to start alone.",
"18v2xhl": "In an observational American study by Jha (NEJM, 2013), people who quit smoking at age 25–34 lived on average about 10 years longer, at 35–44 about 9, at 45–54 about 6 and at 55–64 about 4, compared with those who kept smoking. Quitting before age 40 was linked to avoiding about 90% of the excess risk of death.",
"191h8vw": "In pregnancy and breastfeeding there is no general recommendation here on nicotine replacement or medicines. The decision is made with a doctor or midwife. Do not start nicotine replacement or a medicine before talking to them. In the meantime, support through talking is a step you can start with."
});

